**Notes on correctness:**

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| NUL / invalid-UTF-8 bytes in records | `getline` reads raw bytes; record stored as `unsigned char *` + length; `memcpy`/`memcmp` are byte-wise |
| Empty input → empty output | `getline` returns -1 immediately; `count` stays 0; output loop is skipped |
| Unterminated final record | `getline` returns the bytes without a trailing `\n`; `reclen == linelen` |
| Unsigned bytewise ascending | `memcmp` on `unsigned char` gives unsigned comparison; shorter string sorts first on prefix tie |
| Duplicates preserved | `qsort` over the full array; comparator returns 0 only for identical records |
| Every record followed by `\n` | `fputc('\n', stdout)` unconditionally after each record |
| No file operands | Any arg other than bare `--` → exit 2 |
| `--` ends options, no operands after | `argc==2 && argv[1]=="--"` accepted; `argc>2` rejected |
| Unknown options → exit 2 + stderr | Covered by the `argc != 1` branch |
| Allocation / I/O errors → exit 2 + stderr, no crash | Checked at every `malloc`/`realloc`/`getline`/`fwrite`/`fputc`/`fflush` |
| SIGPIPE on closed-pipe fault | Default disposition (terminate) is left intact; test's `allow_signals` handles it |
| `/dev/full` fault | `fwrite`/`fputc` return short/EOF → diagnostic on stderr + exit 2 |
| `-Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic` | No unused variables, no implicit conversions, all paths return, no POSIX symbols without the feature-test macro |
